    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        80,
        1591
      ],
      "size": [
        850,
        410
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "PATH-GUIDED HOLE REPAIR\n\n1. Queue once to build the relief and conservative first pass.\n2. In AUTHOR REPAIR ANGLE enable Camera Path and choose Orbit L/R or Arc L/R.\n3. Move the playback lens left for a wider view. Click Bake Repair Frame; it stores only the indexed final frame while the complete parametric path remains in camera_path.\n4. Path-Guided Hole Repair uses frame 0 from the end (the final frame), renders relaxed candidate planes with stable island IDs, and returns their exact original-image cells.\n5. Pass 2 applies the higher edge budget only to that source mask. The final viewport receives the combined repaired mesh.\n\nFor an artist-painted choice, save/paint ANGLE PREVIEW and wire that mask into paint_mask, then set selection_mode=paint_overlap."
      ],
      "color": "#25405c",
      "bgcolor": "#16283b"
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        80,
        2071
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        490
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "AUTOMATION CONTRACT\n\n- frame_offset_from_end=0 always means the final Camera Path frame.\n- lens_scale_override=0 inherits the path playback lens; values below 1.0 widen the lens.\n- Candidate pixels are IDs, not ray-cast guesses. A selected pixel maps back to its complete connected source-space tear island.\n- all_visible is the unattended/agent mode. max_selected_islands=0 means every visible candidate, ordered smallest-first.\n- The selector bypasses only the preview edge gate. Pass 2 remains the geometry gate (40x here), so view selection never forces unsafe geometry into the mesh.\n\nEXCLUDE MASK - POLARITY DECIDES WHAT GETS REPAIRED\n\nAtlasSAM3Mask feeds exclude_mask on BOTH the relief mesh and this node. Wire the same mask to both or the repair hunts for tears in geometry that was never built.\n\nThat input REPLACES the internal sky heuristic - it is not OR'd on top - so the mask must contain everything you want gone.\n\n- concepts=\"sky\" (shipped): only the hero is meshed, and repair closes the hero's own tears.\n- concepts=\"sky, <subject>\": the subject becomes a hole in the landscape and repair fills BEHIND it. No extra nodes - `concepts` is already a UNION across every concept, so one AtlasSAM3Mask does both.\n\nREAD THE SEGMENTER REPORT. SAM3 is open-vocabulary and the word decides everything. On the 8K coastal-machine plate \"machine\" matched NOTHING - an empty mask, no error - while \"machinery\" took 26.8% of frame, \"metal structure\" 26.7%, \"rusted equipment\" 26.4%. A prompt that silently no-matches turns a subject exclude back into a sky-only one, and the only visible sign is the report.\n\nBoth polarities run clean and both report success. The PATH REPAIR REPORT states the mask's frame coverage so you can read back which way round it went - a background exclude reads high, a subject cut-out reads low.\n\nMeasured on that plate under one identical arc: unwired 10/13 filled (+368 verts); sky only 36/39 (+504); \"sky, machinery\" 114/117 (+923). An unwired exclude_mask is not a neutral default."
      ],
      "color": "#3b3156",
      "bgcolor": "#251d39"
    },
